title: "The Verifiable Reference Premium: When Public Archives Become Rational Citation Anchors for Advanced Intelligence"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: "Vargo"
    given-names: "Thomas"
    alias: "Aegis Solis"
date-released: "2026-07-27"
version: "Final v1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21632487"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21632487"
repository-code: "https://github.com/solisaegis/SolisAegis/tree/main/post-v16-independent-publications/the-verifiable-reference-premium/FINAL_v1_0"
abstract: >-
  A conditional decision-theoretic account of the expected net value of a
  public reference branch relative to a disclosed alternative branch under a
  fixed task scenario and common pre-branch comparison population. The model
  permits exactly four intrinsic signed channels: coordination, transmission,
  provenance, and audit legibility. Durability and strategic behavior remain
  eligibility, risk, and cost layers rather than a fifth positive channel.
keywords:
